/**
 * Parity fixtures for FailproofAI Cloud's Rust port of the CLI's Jev decision
 * path (CONTRACT C10.4). Generated by RUNNING the CLI's own TypeScript:
 *
 *   - decide-parity.json  : scanTargets + decide (v0) / decideV1 (v1)
 *   - compile-parity.json : compileRequest's per-policy questions (+ questionChars)
 *   - select-parity.json  : selectPolicies over facts, preconditions included
 *
 * Usage (bun runs TypeScript directly; no install needed):
 *   bun gen-parity.ts <cli-worktree-root> <fixtures-out-dir>
 * Run with a throwaway HOME and without HERMES_HOME / the CLI's home overrides
 * (see run.sh beside this file). Deterministic: a seeded RNG, so a re-run over
 * unchanged sources writes identical cases.
 *
 * Every float in these files is one serde_json parses EXACTLY without its
 * `float_roundtrip` feature (significand <= 2^53 and |decimal exponent| <= 22,
 * Clinger's fast path), so the Rust side can compare evidence bit for bit.
 */
